From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:24:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211_hwsim: free a frame whose rate is wider than
 the channel

mac80211_hwsim_tx() warns and returns when a rate of the frame is wider
than the channel width in use, but does not free the frame, so it leaks
the skb and the frame never gets a TX status. Free it as the other drop
paths of the function do.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
@@ -2457,8 +2457,10 @@ static void mac80211_hwsim_tx(struct iee
 		else if (rflags & IEEE80211_TX_RC_160_MHZ_WIDTH)
 			bw = NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_160;
 
-		if (WARN_ON(hwsim_get_chanwidth(bw) > hwsim_get_chanwidth(confbw)))
+		if (WARN_ON(hwsim_get_chanwidth(bw) > hwsim_get_chanwidth(confbw))) {
+			ieee80211_free_txskb(hw, skb);
 			return;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (tx_link_sta && control->sta->valid_links)
